#: ../../source/horloge.rst:4
msgid "Horloge et prévisions"
msgstr "Clock and forecasts"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:10
msgid ""
"``Config.MinPerPoint × n`` minutes (``rules.ExpectedDuration``). Avec le "
"défaut de 8 min/point, un match en 7 points est attendu en 56 minutes. "
"L'étude recommande de compter **11 min/point pour planifier une ronde** "
"(attente comprise) et 8 min/point pour l'espérance d'un match."
msgstr ""
"``Config.MinPerPoint × n`` minutes (``rules.ExpectedDuration``). With the"
" default of 8 min/point, a 7-point match is expected to take 56 minutes. "
"The study recommends counting **11 min/point to plan a round** (waiting "
"included) and 8 min/point for the expectation of a match."

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:18
msgid ""
"Les matchs en cours (``Running()``, dans l'ordre de lancement) dont la "
"durée écoulée ``now - Start`` dépasse strictement ``facteur × "
"Expected(Length)`` (``rules.IsSlow``). Le tableau des matchs en cours de "
"``render`` applique le même critère avec un facteur de 1,5 et marque la "
"ligne (classe CSS ``lent``)."
msgstr ""
"The matches in progress (``Running()``, in start order) whose elapsed "
"duration ``now - Start`` strictly exceeds ``facteur × Expected(Length)`` "
"(``rules.IsSlow``). The ``render`` table of matches in progress applies "
"the same criterion with a factor of 1.5 and marks the row (CSS class "
"``lent``)."

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:35
msgid ""
"Enveloppe de ``rules.PaceAt(s.RulesMatches(), now, start)`` "
"(``rules.Pace`` a les mêmes champs) :"
msgstr ""
"Wrapper of ``rules.PaceAt(s.RulesMatches(), now, start)`` (``rules.Pace``"
" has the same fields):"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:47
msgid ""
"Les matchs gagnés par forfait sont exclus des moyennes : ils fausseraient"
" la mesure."
msgstr ""
"Matches won by forfeit are excluded from the averages: they would skew "
"the measurement."

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:50
msgid "Autres pièces du temps"
msgstr "Other pieces of time"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:57
msgid ""
"Ces deux fonctions donnent aux règles pures de ``rules/prevision.go`` "
"leur entrée :"
msgstr ""
"These two functions give the pure rules of ``rules/prevision.go`` their "
"input:"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:59
msgid ""
"``rules.PlayingTime(matches, now)`` : union des intervalles ``[Start, "
"End)`` des matchs non annulés, jusqu'à ``now`` (un match en cours ou sans"
" fin compte jusqu'à ``now``) ; les trous où aucune table ne jouait ne "
"comptent pas ;"
msgstr ""
"``rules.PlayingTime(matches, now)``: union of the ``[Start, End)`` "
"intervals of non-cancelled matches, up to ``now`` (a match in progress or"
" without an end counts up to ``now``); gaps where no table was playing do"
" not count;"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:62
msgid ""
"``rules.DayOfPlay(start, now)`` : jour calendaire de ``now`` compté "
"depuis celui de ``start`` (1 = le même jour), 0 si ``start`` est nul ;"
msgstr ""
"``rules.DayOfPlay(start, now)``: calendar day of ``now`` counted from "
"that of ``start`` (1 = the same day), 0 if ``start`` is zero;"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:64
msgid ""
"``rules.AfterBreaks(now, play, breaks)`` : l'heure où se termine ``play``"
" posé à partir de ``now``, pauses sautées (une pause en cours retarde le "
"départ, une pause rencontrée ajoute sa longueur ; finir exactement au "
"début d'une pause, c'est finir avant elle) ;"
msgstr ""
"``rules.AfterBreaks(now, play, breaks)``: the time at which ``play`` ends"
" when laid out from ``now``, skipping breaks (a break in progress delays "
"the start, a break encountered adds its length; finishing exactly at the "
"start of a break means finishing before it);"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:67
msgid ""
"``rules.EstimatedEnd(now, remaining, breaks)`` : la médiane des durées "
"restantes simulées (la plus haute des deux du milieu pour un nombre "
"pair), posée après ``now`` par ``AfterBreaks`` ; ``ok`` est faux sans "
"aucune durée."
msgstr ""
"``rules.EstimatedEnd(now, remaining, breaks)``: the median of the "
"simulated remaining durations (the higher of the two middle ones for an "
"even number), laid out after ``now`` by ``AfterBreaks``; ``ok`` is false "
"without any duration."

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:71
msgid ""
"Les durées restantes viennent de ``sim.Forecast`` (voir "
":ref:`simulation`)."
msgstr ""
"The remaining durations come from ``sim.Forecast`` (see "
":ref:`simulation`)."

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:74
msgid "Le temps dans les propositions"
msgstr "Time in proposals"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:76
msgid ""
"Le moteur n'a pas d'horloge : ``ProposeAt(now)`` reçoit l'heure de "
"l'hôte, ``Propose()`` prend ``State.Last`` (horodatage du dernier "
"événement). Deux règles seulement en dépendent :"
msgstr ""
"The engine has no clock: ``ProposeAt(now)`` receives the host's time, "
"``Propose()`` takes ``State.Last`` (timestamp of the last event). Only "
"two rules depend on it:"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:79
msgid ""
"**micro-rondes** (``batch_minutes`` d'un suisse continu) : l'échéance du "
"prochain lot est le départ du dernier match non annulé lancé dans la "
"phase, plus ``batch_minutes`` ; elle n'est stockée nulle part. Le premier"
" lot ne s'attend pas. Avant l'échéance, le moteur propose ``wait`` avec "
"``Reason = waiting_batch`` et ``Until`` = l'échéance ;"
msgstr ""
"**micro-rounds** (``batch_minutes`` of a continuous Swiss): the deadline "
"of the next batch is the start of the last non-cancelled match started in"
" the phase, plus ``batch_minutes``; it is stored nowhere. The first batch"
" is not waited for. Before the deadline, the engine proposes ``wait`` "
"with ``Reason = waiting_batch`` and ``Until`` = the deadline;"

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:83
msgid ""
"**pauses** (``Config.Breaks``, ``TimeRange`` à ``Start`` incluse et "
"``End`` exclue) : une proposition ``start_match`` dont l'intervalle "
"``[now, now + Expected(Length)]`` rencontre une pause porte ``Warn = "
"ends_in_break``. Rien n'est bloqué : le TD décide."
msgstr ""
"**breaks** (``Config.Breaks``, ``TimeRange`` with ``Start`` included and "
"``End`` excluded): a ``start_match`` proposal whose interval ``[now, now "
"+ Expected(Length)]`` meets a break carries ``Warn = ends_in_break``. "
"Nothing is blocked: the TD decides."

#: ../../source/horloge.rst:87
msgid "Voir :ref:`propositions`."
msgstr "See :ref:`propositions`."
